WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.403
A relay station records an integer load for each time slot in the array loads. You may reserve

2
00:00:05.403 --> 00:00:12.198
exactly width consecutive slots. Return the largest total load among all such reservations. Negative values

3
00:00:12.198 --> 00:00:17.821
represent load returned to the station, so a valid answer can be negative. Return the total, not the

4
00:00:17.821 --> 00:00:18.808
starting index.

5
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.730
Slots with zero-based indices 2 through 4 contain 5, 2, and 6; their sum is 13.

6
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:33.563
The two valid totals are -6 and -9. Choosing no slots is not allowed.

7
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.823
Two adjacent windows differ in exactly two positions: one leaves and one enters.

8
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:48.049
Sum the first width entries once. Shift the window by removing the outgoing value and adding the incoming

9
00:00:48.049 --> 00:00:50.865
value. Update the maximum after every shift.

10
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.084
I first considered recomputing each reservation in O(n × width). Adjacent windows share width - 1 entries, so

11
00:00:59.084 --> 00:01:05.795
I maintain one running sum and update only the entering and leaving values. The algorithm takes linear time

12
00:01:05.795 --> 00:01:07.384
and constant extra space.

13
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:13.247
The first three values total 9. Initialize both the current sum and best sum to 9.

14
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:21.046
Move once: subtract 3 and add 2 to obtain 8. Move again: subtract 1 and add 6 to

15
00:01:21.046 --> 00:01:22.076
obtain 13.

16
00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:26.936
The last shift totals 9. The best value remains 13.

17
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:29.460
O(n). O(1)
